---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Privacy policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: your pay stays on your device`} description="What the labor law calculators process: no cookie, no account, no wage, schedule or employer data kept by the publisher. Your rights under the GDPR and US state privacy laws." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. Someone checking whether they were underpaid, or when their last paycheck is due, may be in a dispute with an employer. The calculators were written so that none of that information leaves the browser. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to everything the site does, and the rights it gives are open to every visitor wherever they live.</p>
    <p>This site sets no cookie, and the calculators store nothing on your device.</p>
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What never leaves your browser</h2>
    <p>Your hourly pay, salary, hours and shifts, last day of work, months of service, the size of your employer and anything else you type are processed by code running on your own device. They are never sent to us, to an employer or to an agency. The "copy share link" button puts your figures into the page address so you can send the calculation to someone; whoever receives the link sees them.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>The host records the IP address, time, requested page and browser type of each request to keep the service secure. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention follows the host's policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Anonymous stability monitoring, without cookies</h3><p>To find broken pages, the site loads Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, Dublin) in cookie-free mode: errors, load times, dead clicks and scrolling are measured per page view, without cookies and without linking visits, and page content and everything typed are masked. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a working site.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics</h3><p>No audience measurement, advertising or social media tool runs on this site today. If a stability monitoring tool is added, this page will name it and say what it records before it is switched on.</p></>}
    <h3>Emails</h3><p>If you write to us, we keep your address and message to answer, and delete them three years after the last exchange. Please do not send pay stubs, your employer's name or a case number: the state and the rule you question are enough.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no sharing</h2><p>We do not sell personal information, do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising and do not build profiles.</p>
    <h2>5. Recipients and transfers</h2><p>The host may process request data in the United States under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>You may ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability, or object to processing, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we answer within one month. You may also complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>). Residents of US states with privacy laws have the same rights through the same address.</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>Teen workers are welcome to read the pages; the site collects nothing from anyone, children included.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
